  "body": "## What changed\n\nThe test `a_rough_over_an_oversized_bar_peels_from_the_stock_radius` in `crates/app/tests/rotary_verify.rs` pins the d12.4 matching bar at 2,110 moves. The old pin was 2,064. No production code changes.\n\n## Cause\n\nPR #3496 (merge `6eff704f2`, issue #3168) removes the `seam.is_none()` guard in `machining3d::hsm::plan_level`. Each Auto/Zigzag rotary level now ends with a seam ring. This adds moves on purpose.\n\n## Readings (debug, the test alone, `--exact`)\n\n| Commit | d12.4 bar | d20 bar | Result |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `7868d3786` (`6eff704f2^1`) | 2,064 | 7,648 | pass |\n| `6eff704f2` (merge of #3496) | 2,110 | 7,578 | fail at the 2,064 pin |\n| `436d38ffb` (main) | 2,110 | 7,578 | fail at the 2,064 pin |\n\nAll the safety asserts of the test pass on the new path: no blocking warning, the top level starts at the stock radius, and the program posts. The d20 bar stays under the 9,000-move bound. So the number is obsolete and no rule broke. A revert was dropped: it removes the wall-cusp fix of #3168. The decision is in `docs/decisions/3774-rotary-verify-ring-reading.md`.\n\n## Pinning tests\n\n- `a_rough_over_an_oversized_bar_peels_from_the_stock_radius` - green.\n- The `rotary_verify` binary: 10 passed.\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-app --test rotary_verify -- -D warnings` - clean.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- No heavy lane and no light lane: the PR changes one test number and a decision file.\n- The post-merge `example_catalog` failure on `44e6a8269` (`catalog_3d_rough_finish::regenerates`, slow >60 s) did not recur on the later runs. This PR does not touch it.\n\nChangelog: none\n\nEffort: high\n\nFixes #3774\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
